&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Enlargement of a dwelling house (Class B) &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;- The operations comprising the erection of a hip to gable and rear dormer roof extension, would consist of the enlargement of a dwelling house
within the meaning of Class B of Part 1 of Schedule 2 to the Town &amp;amp; Country
Planning (General Permitted Development)&amp;nbsp;
(England) Order 2015 &quot;the Order&quot; and would comply with the
development tolerances set out in said Class B. The operation would therefore
have been granted planning permission by Article 3 of the Order.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Alteration to the roof of the dwelling house (Class C)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt; - The operations comprising the installation of x3 roof lights to the front roofslope would consist of any other alteration to the roof of the
dwelling house within the meaning of Class C of Part 1 of Schedule 2 to the
Town &amp;amp; Country Planning (General Permitted Development)&amp;nbsp; (England) Order 2015 &quot;the Order&quot;
and would comply with the development tolerances set out in said Class C. The
operation would therefore have been granted planning permission by Article 3 of
